  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\n\nCurrently, `SparseLabelOp.register_length` stores the \"register length\" of the operator. Typically this would be the number of qubits in the operator when it is mapped to qubits. However, as far as I can tell, there is no need to store the register length with the original operator. Instead, the register length can be specified at the time the operator is mapped to qubits. For example,\r\n```python\r\nqubit_op = JordanWigner().map(fermionic_op, register_length=5)\r\n```\r\nIf the register length is not specified, it can be automatically inferred from the indices present in the operator. This approach is more flexible because the user would not need to specify a register length during initialization.",
